faux-person-web is under the MIT License (see LICENSE). The people,
companies and names it serves come from faux-person
(https://github.com/tauasa/faux-person, MIT License), whose data is built
from these sources. faux-person's own NOTICE, in its jar at META-INF/NOTICE,
gives the detail. The page credits them under every table.

1. Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), CC0 1.0: given and family names,
   their spellings in their own scripts, company names, headquarters,
   countries and official websites, and the names and locations of streets
   outside the US.

2. GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org), licensed under the Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):
   the city and state for each ZIP code, company headquarters resolved to a
   city, and the city and postal code nearest each street outside the US.
   Changes: places were sampled per state, joined to postal codes, and
   reduced to name, state and one ZIP code; outside the US, reduced to a
   place name and one postal code per street.

3. US Census Bureau, TIGER/Line Shapefiles 2024, Address Features (ADDRFEAT).
   A work of the US Government, not subject to copyright in the United States.
   Street names and ZIP codes.
